# Dastro 3.2 — manual patch

## 1. Pass `DRAFT_MODE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT` to the dastro config

Dastro 3.2 can turn on draft mode without the draft mode cookie (e.g. on a
pre-launch stage), with a per-browser opt-out. It reads the setting from
`datocms.draftModeEnabledByDefault`, so the project config must pass the env
var through — otherwise it always stays `false`.

In `src/config/dastro.config.ts`, add the import from `astro:env/server`:

```ts
import {
  // ...
  DRAFT_MODE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT,
} from 'astro:env/server';
```

and pass it in the `datocms` section:

```ts
  datocms: {
    // ...
    baseEditingUrl: DATO_CMS_BASE_EDITING_URL,
    draftModeEnabledByDefault: DRAFT_MODE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT,
  },
```

## 2. Add the env var to `.env.example`

Below `ALLOW_DATO_ENVIRONMENT_SWITCH`, add:

```sh
# Show drafts without the draft mode cookie (e.g. pre-launch stage). Ignored when ENVIRONMENT=production.
DRAFT_MODE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT=false
```

## 3. Optional: enable it on Netlify for non-production contexts

New projects created with `dastro create` get this automatically. For an
existing project that should show drafts by default on stage and previews, set
it for the non-production contexts only (it is ignored when
`ENVIRONMENT=production` anyway):

```sh
netlify env:set DRAFT_MODE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT true --context deploy-preview branch-deploy dev
```

Run it in a directory linked to the site (`netlify link`), or prefix it with
`NETLIFY_SITE_ID=<site-id>`. Existing deploys pick it up on the next deploy.
